Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 19:21:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?v0.2.1:=20fix=20read=5Ffrom=20=E2=80=94=20r?=
 =?UTF-8?q?emove=20inline-read,=20always=20pop=5For=5Fwait?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The inline read_from (slow path) in EncryptedPacketConn competed with
the background session_handler_loop for inner_lock and inner.read_from(),
causing massive latency jitter (28→649ms) and 25% packet loss when
only 1 peer was connected.

Root cause: with 7+ mesh peers, the buffer was always full and the
fast path (try_pop) never missed. With 1 peer, try_pop frequently
returned None, triggering the slow path which contended for inner_lock
with the background reader — two tasks racing on the same inner
read_from.

Fix: remove the inline slow path entirely. read_from always blocks
on pop_or_wait from the TrafficBuffer. The background reader is the
sole reader of inner — no lock contention.

Also:
- Removed unused curve_priv from EncryptedPacketConn struct
- Removed inner_lock (no longer needed without inline read)
- Bumped BUFFER_CAPACITY 64→512 (matches original mpsc capacity)
- Added aarch64 cortex-a53 target to .cargo/config.toml
- Bumped version to 0.2.1
